1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,700
It's seven in the morning and these people
have been walking since midnight.

2
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:12,950
13 kilometres along the coast of Kerala,
praying the rosary without ever stopping.

3
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:18,300
The world, told by those who live it.

4
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:20,800
This is Voci Vere.

5
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:24,600
It's called Akhanda Japamala, the unbroken
rosary.

6
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:28,000
It starts from a shrine dedicated to Mary,
in Kalavoor,

7
00:00:28,070 --> 00:00:31,350
and it ends in Arthunkal: 13 kilometres
along the coast.

8
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,750
And the prayer never stops.

9
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:37,000
I'm on the coast of the Indian Ocean, in
Kerala.

10
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:41,300
One of the most famous pilgrimages in
India is about to begin.

11
00:00:42,030 --> 00:00:46,900
Millions of people gathered, walking tens
of kilometres along the coast,

12
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:50,000
to reach the Basilica of Saint Andrew.

13
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:51,750
All of this from midnight.

14
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:59,900
A community that gathers to walk in
devotion to the Blessed Virgin.

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,400
And the local people will prepare food and
drinks to give to the pilgrims.

16
00:01:05,990 --> 00:01:08,000
No one would have guessed it would fill up
during the night.

17
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:21,150
We set off in the dark, no one talks about
anything else.

18
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,950
Whoever leads the rosary says the first
half of the prayer. The others answer.

19
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,200
For kilometres.

20
00:01:27,310 --> 00:01:29,500
The prayer passes from one group to the
next, without a gap.

21
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:40,400
Hundreds of thousands of people.

22
00:01:40,470 --> 00:01:43,000
The first time, in 2002, there were a few
hundred.

23
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:46,900
As they told us, it starts from a shrine
dedicated to Mary, in Kalavoor,

24
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:50,500
for 13-14 kilometres, all the way to
Arthunkal.

25
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:58,200
We're in Marari, on the coast of Kerala.

26
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:03,800
They used to do it all on the road, but
the traffic caused too much chaos,

27
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,800
so they moved straight onto the beach.

28
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,200
And there it carries on along the beach.

29
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:11,200
Some come for faith, some for a promise,
some because their father did it before them.

30
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:12,900
The road is the same for everyone.

31
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,700
What does it mean for you?

32
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:17,550
So this is basically a rally which happens
every year.

33
00:02:17,550 --> 00:02:22,150
It's based on the apparition of Mother
Mary, which happened in Alappuzha.

34
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:26,050
Since October is the month of Mother Mary,
we dedicate this month to the rally.

35
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:28,650
And about four lakh people take part in
this.

36
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:33,950
It's just like giving a devotion to Mother
Mary.

37
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,900
She has given me a lot of blessings in my
life.

38
00:02:36,950 --> 00:02:38,200
Through Jesus Christ.

39
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:39,200
I'm twenty-six.

40
00:02:39,250 --> 00:02:40,050
This is the first time here.

41
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,750
And for you, is it the first time?

42
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,450
No.

43
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,100
This is faith and belief.

44
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:49,900
There are so many miracles happening
there.

45
00:02:49,950 --> 00:02:54,400
Those who are taking part in this, they
have something in it.

46
00:02:54,450 --> 00:02:55,900
Some happiness.

47
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:59,500
And it's not only people walking. There
are also those who don't walk.

48
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:02,600
At the side of the road, with big pots and
glasses of water.

49
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:05,300
They give food and drink to anyone passing
by.

50
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:07,200
Without asking for anything in return.

51
00:03:07,790 --> 00:03:11,700
Some pray, some watch from their homes,
some offer water and some are just curious.

52
00:03:14,870 --> 00:03:17,800
This was a stop inside, to drink and eat a
little something.

53
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:19,200
Volunteers, women and men.

54
00:03:20,390 --> 00:03:24,400
Hindu volunteers, helping out at a
Catholic feast too.

55
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:26,300
The ambulance is coming.

56
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:31,150
Truly a community coming together.

57
00:03:31,630 --> 00:03:35,300
Let's try to join them for a little while,
respecting the tradition.

58
00:03:35,790 --> 00:03:37,700
The sun rises and the road doesn't empty.

59
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:50,300
The closer you get, the slower you go.

60
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,800
And after kilometres of walking...

61
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,200
we made it.

62
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:20,900
Now that the whole pilgrimage is over.

63
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:27,400
In Kerala, Christianity is ancient.

64
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:31,800
Tradition says it arrived with the apostle
Thomas, in 52 AD.

65
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:35,500
This church was rebuilt in 1584

66
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:39,200
by an Italian Jesuit, Father Giacomo
Fenicio.

67
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:41,800
Here they still call him Veluthachan,

68
00:04:41,850 --> 00:04:43,100
the white father.

69
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:46,600
In 1647 a statue of Saint Sebastian
arrived from Milan.

70
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:55,400
Since then Arthunkal has been a shrine, and in
January its feast brings people here from all over Kerala.

71
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:11,800
It's boiling hot, really humid, you can
really feel it.

72
00:05:19,550 --> 00:05:21,700
I came to Kerala to listen to the people
who live here.

73
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:25,400
I found myself inside 13 kilometres, next
to people I didn't know,

74
00:05:26,050 --> 00:05:27,700
who gave us something to drink without
asking for anything.

75
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:30,800
Because travelling doesn't only mean
seeing new places.

76
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:35,700
It also means stopping to listen to
stories we would never have known otherwise.

77
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:38,900
The journey of Voci Vere, giving a voice
to those who need it most.

78
00:05:38,950 --> 00:05:40,900
Follow me to discover the next stories.
